1. obra/superpowers (https://github.com/obra/superpowers)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following skills under skills/ are derivative works adapted from the
"superpowers" Claude Code plugin (v5.1.0), originally authored by Jesse Vincent
and contributors:

    skills/ddt-brainstorming/                  (← superpowers/brainstorming)
    skills/ddt-writing-plans/                  (← superpowers/writing-plans)
    skills/ddt-subagent-driven/                (← superpowers/subagent-driven-development)
    skills/ddt-executing-plans/                (← superpowers/executing-plans)
    skills/ddt-tdd/                            (← superpowers/test-driven-development)
    skills/ddt-systematic-debugging/           (← superpowers/systematic-debugging)
    skills/ddt-verification/                   (← superpowers/verification-before-completion)
    skills/ddt-requesting-review/              (← superpowers/requesting-code-review)
    skills/ddt-receiving-review/               (← superpowers/receiving-code-review)
    skills/ddt-dispatching-parallel-agents/    (← superpowers/dispatching-parallel-agents)
    skills/ddt-finishing-a-development-branch/ (← superpowers/finishing-a-development-branch)
    skills/ddt-using-git-worktrees/            (← superpowers/using-git-worktrees)
    skills/ddt-writing-skills/                 (← superpowers/writing-skills)

Adaptation summary:
  - Renamed (slug prefix `ddt-`) to avoid command/skill namespace collisions
    when both plugins are installed.
  - Some skills carry small DDT-context additions in the body (e.g. the
    big-requirement entry split in ddt-brainstorming). Original
    method/checklist/red-flag content is preserved verbatim.

